To build a container image from a Git repository using a Containerfile and deploy it directly onto OpenShift, you can construct a Pipeline utilizing OpenShift's built-in ClusterTasks.
1]git-clone (ClusterTask) to pull down your code into a shared workspace.
2] buildah (ClusterTask) to detect and execute the build based on your Containerfile.
3] openshift-client (ClusterTask) to deploy the newly built image as a live OpenShift Deployment

